      "seed": 1618226578,
      "version": 1683,
      "versionNonce": 315631168,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786686114854,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- call use techique like chunking to break file into smaller pieces and upload independently\n-- chunking happen in client before it send to server\n-- user resume upload, we could check chunks field to see which chunk has been upload and which hasn't\n-- to keep chunks field in sync:\n---> can implement server-side verification of chunk uploads using ETags.\n---> can leverage S3 multipart upload\n--> verify these ETags by calling S3's ListParts API, \nproviding an efficient way to validate multiple chunks at once.\n\n\n--  Content-Defined Chunking (CDC), where chunk boundaries are determined by the file's content \nusing a rolling hash (like Rabin fingerprinting). With CDC, \na small edit only affects the chunks immediately surrounding the change, \nthe vast majority of chunks remain identical. \nThis is how systems like Dropbox actually achieve efficient delta sync in practice.\n-- Also can utilize compression to speed up upload/download. compression is only useful\nif speed gained from transferring fewer bytes outweight time it take to compress\nand decompress the file\n\n\n-- ensure file are secure and only accessible to authorized users\n1. Generation: signURL on server, include URL path, expiration timestamp,\nrestriction (IP address, etc..)\n2. Distribution: signedURL distributed to authorized user, \n3. Validation: check signRUL< verify public key, timestamp expiration and other restriction",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- call use techique like chunking to break file into smaller pieces and upload independently\n-- chunking happen in client before it send to server\n-- user resume upload, we could check chunks field to see which chunk has been upload and which hasn't\n-- to keep chunks field in sync:\n---> can implement server-side verification of chunk uploads using ETags.\n---> can leverage S3 multipart upload\n--> verify these ETags by calling S3's ListParts API, \nproviding an efficient way to validate multiple chunks at once.\n\n\n--  Content-Defined Chunking (CDC), where chunk boundaries are determined by the file's content \nusing a rolling hash (like Rabin fingerprinting). With CDC, \na small edit only affects the chunks immediately surrounding the change, \nthe vast majority of chunks remain identical. \nThis is how systems like Dropbox actually achieve efficient delta sync in practice.\n-- Also can utilize compression to speed up upload/download. compression is only useful\nif speed gained from transferring fewer bytes outweight time it take to compress\nand decompress the file\n\n\n-- ensure file are secure and only accessible to authorized users\n1. Generation: signURL on server, include URL path, expiration timestamp,\nrestriction (IP address, etc..)\n2. Distribution: signedURL distributed to authorized user, \n3. Validation: check signRUL< verify public key, timestamp expiration and other restriction",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
